   "confidence": "medium",
   "notes": "9 Trinity Street, Whistles (sign + fascia lettering in photos). Plain Georgian front of brown/buff stock brick, three storeys: painted white timber shopfront with pilasters (wide display window at north end, glazed door in 2nd bay, two narrower windows south), moulded white cornice over fascia; four white-framed 6/6 sashes on each upper floor in plain openings, simple cornice and parapet at top (roof line only partly seen). x=0 is the north end (next to the gothic yellow-brick building), x=7.51 abuts the stone St Michael's Court (Caius) to the south. Window x positions estimated through perspective; brick colour corrected for shade."
